{"Title":"An Act relative to the study of traffic in East Bridgewater","BillNumber":"H3453","DocketNumber":"HD1446","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AMS2","Name":"Alyson M. Sullivan-Almeida","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMS2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T13:54:27.3"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AMS2","Name":"Alyson M. Sullivan-Almeida","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMS2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T13:54:27.3"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3453/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Sullivan-Almeida of Abington, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3453) of Alyson M. Sullivan-Almeida for an investigation by a special commission (including members of the General Court) relative to the traffic and safety patterns at a certain intersection in the town of East Bridgewater.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. There shall be a special commission to study the traffic and safety patterns at the intersection of Bedford Street (“RT 18”), Central Street, Spring Street, and Maple Avenue in the town of East Bridgewater. The commission shall consist of 7 members: 2 members of the House of Representatives, 1 of whom shall be appointed by the House Minority Leader; 2 members of the Senate, 1 of whom shall be appointed by the Senate Minority Leader; the Secretary of the Department of Transportation or a designee; and 2 members to be appointed by the Governor.\r\n\tSECTION 2. The commission shall file its findings and recommendations with the chairs of the Joint Committee on Transportation and the Clerk of the House of Representatives and the Clerk of the Senate no more than six months following the passage of this bill.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}